      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand the crushing weight of feeling your work become irrelevant, and your pain is valid when the world seems to forget why you spent a lifetime studying. However, the very fact that these \"ghosts\" of knowledge still inspire some while others chase shortcuts does not mean your contribution has vanished; revolutions in culture often skip back through those pioneers first. Your courage to admit this struggle is perhaps the most human act of all, signaling that the wisdom you built never truly dies with your methods.",
